n", meaning := "Whether an implementation-defined debugging facility is available and enabled. A host whose answer is *true* runs DebuggerAction, which the invariants of the essential internal methods bound (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-invariants-of-the-essential-internal-methods\"></emu-xref>)." }, { sig := "DebuggerAction(): ~unused~", meaning := "An implementation-defined debugging action. An implementation must not allow the invariants of the essential internal methods to be circumvented in any manner (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-invariants-of-the-essential-internal-methods\"></emu-xref>), and the model reads this as: every object stays an object and keeps its internal slots but [[Extensible]] and [[Prototype]]; its [[Extensible]] only turns from *true* to *false*; an object whose [[Extensible]] is not *true* keeps its [[Prototype]] and gains no property; and a non-configurable property stays, its attributes changing only as the invariants of [[GetOwnProperty]] allow." }, { sig := "NativeFunctionSource(_func_: a function object): a String", meaning := "An implementation-defined String source code representation of _func_. The representation must have the syntax of a |NativeFunction|. If _func_ has an [[InitialName]] internal slot, _func_.[[InitialName]] is a String, and _func_.[[InitialName]] is matched by |NativeFunctionAccessor?| |PropertyName|, the portion of the returned String that would be matched by |NativeFunctionAccessor?| |PropertyName| must be _func_.[[InitialName]]; a String is so matched when it is *\"get\"* or *\"set\"* (the portion is the name whether it is read as the |NativeFunctionAccessor| or as the |PropertyName|), or when the |NativeFunction| that follows `function ` with it has it as that portion. If _func_.[[InitialName]] is the empty String, the returned String has neither a |NativeFunctionAccessor| nor a |PropertyName|, so that its portion is empty (<emu-xref href=\"#erratum-NativeFunctionInitialName\"></emu-xref>). The returned String is the string