orm of the |Pattern| that _flags_ selects, equivalent to _pattern_ interpreted as UTF-16 encoded Unicode code points, in which certain code points are escaped. The Abstract Closure that would result from evaluating it as that |Pattern| must behave identically to the one _pattern_ gives, and the string-concatenation of *\"/\"*, it, *\"/\"*, and _flags_ must be parsable as a |RegularExpressionLiteral| whose body it is. It is a function of _pattern_ and _flags_: multiple calls with the same values produce identical results." }, { sig := "ForInStep(_obj_: an Object, _history_: a List of Records): a Record", meaning := "The host's next action in enumerating the properties of _obj_, given _history_, a Record { [[Action]], [[Result]] } for each action so far, in order: the action and the result of the internal method call it made, or ~empty~ for a key it returned. The action is a new Record { [[Kind]], [[Object]], [[Key]] }: [[Kind]] is ~own-property-keys~ (call [[OwnPropertyKeys]] of [[Object]]), ~get-own-property~ (call [[GetOwnProperty]] of [[Object]] with [[Key]]), ~get-prototype-of~ (call [[GetPrototypeOf]] of [[Object]]), ~yield~ (return the String [[Key]]) or ~done~ (the enumeration is over); fields an action does not use are ~empty~. The actions conform to the rules of EnumerateObjectProperties." }, { sig := "TerminalAlternatives(_nt_: a nonterminal): a List of Strings", meaning := "A new List of the String values of the code points of each terminal that is a right-hand side of _nt_, whose right-hand sides are each one terminal written in a fixed-width font (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-grammar-notation\"></emu-xref>), in the order the grammar lists them." }, { sig := "SetFieldNamed(_r_: a Record or an Object, _f_: a field name, _v_: anything): ~unused~", meaning := "Sets _r_'s field, or _r_'s internal slot, named _f_ to _v_." }, { sig := "HostSupportsOptional(_c_: a clause): a Boolean", meaning := "Whether a host that is not a web browser provides the normative optional feature that clause _c_ specifies. It is a fact of the host: every call with the same _c_ gives the same answer." }, { sig := "IsIntrinsicName(_n_: a String): a Boolean", meaning := "Whether _n_ is this specification's name of an intrinsic object (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-well-known-intrinsic-objects\"></emu-xref>): a name listed in the “Intrinsic Name” column of <emu-xref href=\"#table-well-known-intrinsic-objects\"></emu-xref>, or such a name with the enclosing % around it extended by one or more parts *\".\"* _k_, each _k_ the key of a property, specified for the object the name before it names, whose value (an accessor property's: its getter's result, as if accessed before any code is evaluated) is an object." }, { sig := "TableAssociated(_t_: a table, _key_: anything): anything", meaning := "The value associated with _key_ in _t_, a step's table of two columns (\"the abstract operation associated with _key_ in the following table\"): the entry in the second column of the row whose entry in the first column is _key_. A sequence of Unicode code points _key_ is the entry written in code as those code points. _t_ has such a row." }, { sig := "WellKnownSymbol(_d_: a String): a Symbol", meaning := "The well-known symbol whose [[Description]] is _d_ (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-well-known-symbols\"></emu-xref>, <emu-xref href=\"#table-well-known-symbols\"></emu-xref>): the value the specification names %_d_%. It is the same value in every realm." }, { sig := "DesignateShared(_block_: a Data Block): a Shared Data Block", meaning := "_block_, a Data Block that no value refers to yet, designated a Shared Data Block (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-data-blocks\"></emu-xref>): from then on it is a Shared Data Block, with the same bytes." }, { sig := "LocaleUppercase(_cps_: a List of code points): a List of code points", meaning := "A new List of the code points of _cps_ mapped to upper case by the conventions of the host environment's current locale (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-string.prototype.tolocaleuppercase\"></emu-xref>): toUppercase(_cps_), except in the few cases (such as Turkish) where the rules for that language conflict with the regular Unicode case mappings." }, { sig := "LocaleLowercase(_cps_: a List of code points): a List of code points", meaning := "A new List of the code points of _cps_ mapped to lower case by the conventions of the host environment's current locale (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-string.prototype.tolocalelowercase\"></emu-xref>): toLowercase(_cps_), except in the few cases (such as Turkish) where the rules for that language conflict with the regular Unicode case mappings." }, { sig := "LocaleCompare(_string_: a String, _thatValue_: a String): a Number", meaning := "The result, other than *NaN*, of an implementation-defined locale-sensitive comparison of _string_ with _thatValue_ (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-string.prototype.localecompare\"></emu-xref>): negative when _string_ is ordered before _thatValue_, positive when it is ordered after, and zero otherwise, by an ordering of all Strings that every call follows (a consistent comparator defining a total ordering); *+0*<sub>𝔽</sub> when the two are canonically equivalent according to the Unicode Standard. It has no effect on ECMAScript state." }, { sig := "LocaleNumberString(_x_: a Number or a BigInt): a String or ~empty~", meaning := "A String that represents _x_ formatted according to the conventions of the host environment's current locale, or ~empty~ where the host returns the same thing as `toString` (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-number.prototype.tolocalestring\"></emu-xref>, <emu-xref href=\"#sec-bigint.prototype.tolocalestring\"></emu-xref>). It has no effect on ECMAScript state." }, { sig := "CanonicalPropertyValue(_p_: a List of code points or a String, _v_: a List of code points or a String): a List of code points", meaning := "A new List of the code points of the canonical property value of _v_ for the Unicode property named _p_: the long name of the row of PropertyValueAliases.txt for _p_ that lists _v_. A pair for which IsPropertyValueAlias(_p_, _v_) is *false* is a sort error." }, { sig := "LocaleDateString(_portion_: a portion (~date~, ~time~ or ~all~), _thisValue_: an ECMAScript language value): a String, ~empty~ or ~throw~", meaning := "A String that represents the “date” portion (~date~), the “time” portion (~time~) or the whole (~all~) of the Date _thisValue_ in the current time zone in a convenient, human-readable form that corresponds to the conventions of the host environment's current locale, or ~empty~ where the host returns the form `toDateString`, `toTimeString` or `toString` returns (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-date.prototype.tolocaledatestring\"></emu-xref>, <emu-xref href=\"#sec-date.prototype.tolocaletimestring\"></emu-xref>, <emu-xref href=\"#sec-date.prototype.tolocalestring\"></emu-xref>). These methods are not generic: their *this* value \"must be an object that has a [[DateValue]] internal slot\" (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-properties-of-the-date-prototype-object\"></emu-xref>), and the text gives no consequence for any other value, for which the host gives a String or ~throw~ (a *TypeError*, as every algorithmic Date method throws); ~empty~ only for an object with a [[DateValue]] internal slot. It has no effect on ECMAScript state." }, { sig := "SuspendAgentUntil(_waiterList_: a WaiterList Record, _timeoutTime_: an extended mathematical value): ~unused~", meaning := "Suspends the surrounding agent until the time is _timeoutTime_, or until another agent performs NotifyWaiter(_waiterList_, _w_) for a Waiter Record _w_ whose [[AgentSignifier]] is the surrounding agent's signifier (via a call to `Atomics.notify`), whichever comes first (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-suspendthisagent\"></emu-xref> step 7). The suspension takes effect together with the LeaveCriticalSection(_waiterList_) performed just before it, in such a way that a notification that arrives after the critical section is exited but before the suspension takes effect is not lost. With the surrounding agent the only agent, it wakes only by the timeout, so never where _timeoutTime_ is +∞." }, { sig := "", meaning := "" }, { sig := "ExpandedYearForm(_tv_: a finite time value): a Boolean", meaning := "Whether the host writes the year of _tv_, one from 0 to 9999, as an expanded year (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-expanded-years\"></emu-xref>) in the String toISOString returns: `YYYY` is \"four decimal digits from 0000 to 9999, or as an expanded year\" (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-date-time-string-format\"></emu-xref>), and toISOString's step 7 does not say which. A year outside that interval is always expanded. It has no effect on ECMAScript state." }, { sig := "HostExtendIntrinsics(_realm_: a Realm Record): ~unused~", meaning := "Provides any properties not described in this specification, and values for them, for _realm_'s intrinsics, the objects its [[Intrinsics]] holds and the objects their properties hold (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-conformance\"></emu-xref>, <emu-xref href=\"#sec-hosts-and-implementations\"></emu-xref>): it only adds own properties to those objects, and may create new values for them; it changes no internal slot, no existing property and no other value, adds no own property to an object whose [[Extensible]] is not *true* (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-invariants-of-the-essential-internal-methods\"></emu-xref>), and adds no own property that <emu-xref href=\"#sec-forbidden-extensions\"></emu-xref> forbids (*\"caller\"* or *\"arguments\"* on a function object)." }, { sig := "HostExtendObject(_o_: an Object): ~unused~", meaning := "Provides any properties not described in this specification, and values for them, for the object _o_ that the specification's steps have just created (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-conformance\"></emu-xref>): it only adds own properties to _o_, and may create new values for them; it changes no internal slot, no existing property and no other value, adds no own property if _o_.[[Extensible]] is not *true* (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-invariants-of-the-essential-internal-methods\"></emu-xref>), and adds no own property that <emu-xref href=\"#sec-forbidden-extensions\"></emu-xref> forbids." }, { sig := "OnContextStack(_ctx_: an execution context): a Boolean", meaning := "Whether _ctx_ is an element of the execution context stack (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-execution-contexts\"></emu-xref>)." }, { sig := "HostJobCallbackData(_callback_: a function object): anything", meaning := "The host's [[HostDefined]] value of the JobCallback Record HostMakeJobCallback makes for _callback_ (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-hostmakejobcallback\"></emu-xref>): ~empty~ in the default implementation. It changes only the heap, each object as <emu-xref href=\"#sec-invariants-of-the-essential-internal-methods\"></emu-xref> allows; it may create new values." }, { sig := "HostPrepareCallJobCallback(_jobCallback_: a JobCallback Record): ~unused~", meaning := "The host's steps before HostCallJobCallback calls _jobCallback_.[[Callback]] (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-hostcalljobcallback\"></emu-xref>; HTML's preparation to run a callback): none in the default implementation. They change only the heap, the execution context stack and the suspended context, each object as <emu-xref href=\"#sec-invariants-of-the-essential-internal-methods\"></emu-xref> allows." }, { sig := "HostCleanupCallJobCallback(_jobCallback_: a JobCallback Record): ~unused~", meaning := "The host's steps after HostCallJobCallback's call of _jobCallback_.[[Callback]] returns (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-hostcalljobcallback\"></emu-xref>; HTML's clean-up after running a callback): none in the default implementation. They change only the heap, the execution context stack and the suspended context, each object as <emu-xref href=\"#sec-invariants-of-the-essential-internal-methods\"></emu-xref> allows." }, { sig := "ReplacedSourceText(_node_: a Parse Node, _replacement_: a String): a sequence of Unicode code points", meaning := "A new sequence of the code points of the source text that the root Parse Node of the parser invocation that made _node_ matched (the white space and comments before its first and after its last input element left out, which give no Early Errors), with the source text that _node_ matched replaced by the code points of _replacement_ (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-stringtocodepoints\"></emu-xref>). The source text of a cover's reparse is the source text the covering node matched, in the source text of the invocation that made the covering node, and so on through every cover (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-static-semantic-rules\"></emu-xref>); the |IfStatement| a node of <emu-xref href=\"#sec-functiondeclarations-in-ifstatement-statement-clauses\"></emu-xref>'s productions is processed as matched that node's source text with a `{` before and a `}` after each |FunctionDeclaration| child, and a point of its source text is the point of the node's source text it stands at, the braces left out." }, { sig := "SwitchToAgent(_agent_: an Agent Record): ~unused~", meaning := "Saves the execution context stack in the surrounding agent's Agent Record's [[ParkedStack]], makes _agent_.[[ParkedStack]] the execution context stack and _agent_ the surrounding agent. The execution context that was running before is the one whose evaluation a following Resume suspends. _agent_ is not the surrounding agent, and the surrounding agent is in no critical section." }, { sig := "HostSelectAgent(_agent_: an Agent Record, _n_: a non-negative integer): an Agent Record or ~empty~", meaning := "The host's choice of the agent of _agent_'s agent cluster that runs next, after _agent_ has added _n_ events to its [[EventList]]: an agent other than _agent_ that is not suspended or has been woken, or ~empty~ if the host lets _agent_ continue (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-forward-progress\"></emu-xref>)." }, { sig := "AgentTimeout(): a non-negative integer", meaning := "The time the host advances the agent cluster's clock to while no other agent can run and the surrounding agent is suspended: the