/emu-xref>): the scheduling of a Job of this agent, ready to be performed now, that has not been taken, else ~empty~. The scheduling is identified by an integer the host gives; taking it is taking that Job." }, { sig := "AgentPrepareJob(_k_: a non-negative integer): a Job Abstract Closure", meaning := "Performs the host-defined preparation steps of the Job the scheduling _k_ scheduled, with the execution context stack empty, and returns that Job." }, { sig := "AgentCleanupJob(_k_: a non-negative integer): ~unused~", meaning := "Performs the host-defined cleanup steps of the Job the scheduling _k_ scheduled; the execution context stack is then empty." }, { sig := "", meaning := "" }, { sig := "", meaning := "" }, { sig := "", meaning := "" }, { sig := "", meaning := "" }, { sig := "ApproxPower(_base_: a Number, _exponent_: a Number): a Number", meaning := "An implementation-approximated Number value representing the result of raising ℝ(_base_) to the ℝ(_exponent_) power: the host's choice, as for an implementation-approximated Number value (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-numeric-types-number-exponentiate\"></emu-xref> step 13). The step calls it with finite Numbers other than *+0*<sub>𝔽</sub> and *-0*<sub>𝔽</sub>, _base_ positive or _exponent_ integral." }, { sig := "BigIntTooLarge(_operation_: a String, _x_: a BigInt, _y_: a BigInt): a Boolean", meaning := "Whether the BigInt that the BigInt type's numeric method named _operation_ (*\"exponentiate\"*, *\"leftShift\"* or *\"multiply\"*) returns for _x_ and _y_ would exceed the implementation's maximum BigInt size: the host's choice. The specification sets no maximum (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-ecmascript-language-types-bigint-type\"></emu-xref>: \"The value may be any size and is not limited to a particular bit-width\"); the proposed reading of erratum BigIntMaximumSize asks it." }, { sig := "HasUseStrictDirective(_body_: a |FunctionBody| or |ScriptBody| Parse Node): a Boolean", meaning := "Whether the Directive Prologue of _body_