ng value that is made from _n_ copies of _s_ appended together: the string-concatenation of _n_ copies of _s_, the empty String for _n_ = 0 (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-ecmascript-language-types-string-type\"></emu-xref>)." }, { sig := "ParseNodesWithin(_node_: a Parse Node): a List of Parse Nodes", meaning := "A new List of _node_ and the Parse Nodes of nonterminals that it contains, in source text order with a node before its children (the model's descendants of _node_, after _node_); « _node_ » for a terminal's Parse Node. The Parse Nodes contained within _node_ include _node_: CountLeftCapturingParensWithin(|Atom|) of an |Atom| that is itself a left-capturing parenthesis counts it, as RepeatMatcher's clearing of the captures of the quantified |Atom| needs. Every phrase that reads the List asks for instances of a nonterminal or a production, so terminals' Parse Nodes are not listed." }, { sig := "ListFindOf(_t_: a type, _f_: a field name, _l_: a List, _v_: anything): anything", meaning := "ListFind(_f_, _l_, _v_) among the elements of _l_ of the Record sort _t_: the element of _l_ that is a _t_ and whose _f_ field is _v_. Exactly one element of _l_ is a _t_ with an _f_ field whose value is _v_." }, { sig := "NumberDigitsExponent(_x_: a Number, _radix_: an integer): an integer", meaning := "The _n_ of the integers _n_, _k_ and _s_ that Number::toString's step <emu-xref href=\"#step-number-tostring-intermediate-values\"></emu-xref> lets be such that _k_ ≥ 1, _radix_<sup>_k_ - 1</sup> ≤ _s_ &lt; _radix_<sup>_k_</sup>, 𝔽(_s_ × _radix_<sup>_n_ - _k_</sup>) is _x_, and _k_ is as small as possible, for a finite Number _x_ > *+0*<sub>𝔽</sub> and _radix_ in the inclusive interval from 2 to 36. The three integers are the implementation's function of _x_ and _radix_: where the condition leaves the least significant digit of _s_ open, the implementation's choice, the same at every call." }, { sig := "NumberDigitsCount(_x_: a Number, _radix_: an integer): a positive integer", meaning := "The _k_ of the same three integers as NumberDigitsExponent(_x_, _radix_): the number of digits of _s_." }, { sig := "NumberDigitsSignificand(_x_: a Number, _radix_: an integer): a positive integer", meaning := "The _s_ of the same three integers as NumberDigitsExponent(_x_, _radix_)." }, { sig := "DecimalExponent(_x_: a mathematical value): an integer", meaning := "The integer _e_ such that 10<sup>_e_</sup> ≤ _x_ &lt; 10<sup>_e_ + 1</sup>, for _x_ > 0: the place of the first significant digit of the decimal representation of _x_ (the units digit's is 0)." }, { sig := "EmptyCharSet(): a CharSet", meaning := "A new empty CharSet." }, { sig := "CharSetInterval(_i_: a non-negative integer, _j_: a non-negative integer): a CharSet", meaning := "A new CharSet containing all characters whose character value is in the inclusive interval from _i_ to _j_." }, { sig := "CharSetMinus(_a_: a CharSet, _b_: a CharSet): a CharSet", meaning := "A new CharSet containing the CharSetElements of _a_ that are not also CharSetElements of _b_." }, { sig := "CharSetAllSingle(_cs_: a CharSet): a Boolean", meaning := "Whether every CharSetElement of _cs_ consists of a single character." }, { sig := "CharSetSingles(_cs_: a CharSet): a CharSet", meaning := "A new CharSet containing every CharSetElement of _cs_ that consists of a single character." }, { sig := "CharSetNoScf(): a CharSet", meaning := "A new CharSet containing all Unicode code points _c_ that do not have a Simple Case Folding mapping (scf(_c_) = _c_)." }, { sig := "CharSetCanonExtra(_cs_: a CharSet, _u_: a Boolean): a CharSet", meaning := "A new CharSet containing the characters _c_ not in _cs_ whose case-folded Canonicalize(_c_, _u_) is in _cs_." }, { sig := "CharSetHasCanonical(_cs_: a CharSet, _cc_: a character, _u_: a Boolean, _ic_: a Boolean): a Boolean", meaning := "Whether _cs_ contains a single-character CharSetElement _a_ whose Canonicalize(_a_, _u_, _ic_) is _cc_." }, { sig := "IsCharSet(_v_: anything): a Boolean", meaning := "Whether _v_ is a CharSet (<emu-xref href=\"#sec-pattern-notation\"></emu-xref>)." }, { sig := "IntToRadix(_n_: a non-negative integer, _radix_: an integer): a String", meaning := "The representation of _n_ using radix _radix_ in positional notation without leading zeroes, with digits from the first _radix_ code units of *\"0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\"*, for _n_ ≥ 0 and _radix_ in the inclusive interval from 2 to 36." }, { sig := "StringTooLarge(_len_: a non-negative integer): a Boolean", meaning := "Host-defined (under erratum StringMaximumLength): whether a String of length _len_ exceeds the implementation's maximum String length (at most 2<sup>53</sup> - 1; <emu-xref href=\"#sec-ecmascript-language-types-string-type\"></emu-xref>)." }]

